{"case_id": "E12", "patient_id": "E12", "flags": [{"flag_type": "interaction", "drugs": ["amiodarone", "simvastatin"], "explanation": "The patient is taking 40 mg of simvastatin daily while on amiodarone. The amiodarone label states that the coadministered dose of simvastatin should be limited to 20 mg.", "is_problem": true, "severity": "major", "recommendation": "Limit the coadministered dose of simvastatin to 20 mg.", "citations": [{"chunk_id": "amiodarone::drug_interactions::01", "quote": "Increased plasma concentration of HMG-CoA reductase inhibitor. Limit the dose of lovastatin to 40 mg. Limit the coadministered dose of simvastatin to 20 mg.", "verified": true, "drug": "amiodarone", "field": "drug_interactions", "dailymed_url": "https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/lookup.cfm?setid=0caedb97-56fd-4ec0-bfb2-c7683b8f5f1b"}]}, {"flag_type": "interaction", "drugs": ["amiodarone", "warfarin"], "explanation": "Amiodarone potentiates the anticoagulant response of warfarin. The label recommends reducing the warfarin dose by one-third to one-half and monitoring prothrombin times.", "is_problem": true, "severity": "major", "recommendation": "Reduce warfarin dose by one-third to one-half and monitor prothrombin times.", "citations": [{"chunk_id": "amiodarone::drug_interactions::01", "quote": "Potentiates anticoagulant response and can result in serious or fatal bleeding. Coadministration increases prothrombin time by 100% after 3 to 4 days. Reduce warfarin dose by one-third to one-half and monitor prothrombin times.", "verified": true, "drug": "amiodarone", "field": "drug_interactions", "dailymed_url": "https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/lookup.cfm?setid=0caedb97-56fd-4ec0-bfb2-c7683b8f5f1b"}]}, {"flag_type": "interaction", "drugs": ["omeprazole", "warfarin"], "explanation": "Concomitant use of omeprazole and warfarin may increase INR and prothrombin time, potentially leading to abnormal bleeding.", "is_problem": true, "severity": "moderate", "recommendation": "Monitor